.TH "CSSMATHMAX" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSMathMax \- CSSMathMax
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSMathMax\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed Object
Model API represents the CSS \f[CR]max()\f[R] function.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathMax()\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
Creates a new \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R] object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Also inherits properties from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathMax.values\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]CSSNumericArray\f[R] object which contains one or more
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] objects.
.SH STATIC METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The CSS \f[CR]max()\f[R] function takes one or more comma\-separated
values as arguments and returns the largest of them.
.PP
If all arguments are absolute values, such as pixel lengths,
\f[CR]max()\f[R] is resolved to a single value at parse time,
represented by the CSS Typed Object Model as a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R].
If the \f[CR]max()\f[R] expression can\(cqt be resolved to a single
value at parse time (say, because one of its arguments uses a relative
unit like \f[CR]vw\f[R] or \f[CR]%\f[R]), the function is represented as
a \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R] object, and the arguments passed to
\f[CR]max()\f[R] (or to the \f[CR]CSSMathMax()\f[R] constructor) are
exposed as the \f[CR]values\f[R] property.
.PP
Note that \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R] represents the \f[CR]max()\f[R]
function, not its resolved value.
In order to determine the value of a property using \f[CR]max()\f[R],
you need to read its computed style (for example with
\f[CR]getComputedStyle()\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The following code creates a \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R] instance from three
values, then reads back its \f[CR]operator\f[R] and \f[CR]values\f[R]
properties.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] max = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSMathMax(CSS.px(10), CSS.em(5), CSS.percent(50));

console.log(max.constructor.name); \f[I]// \(dqCSSMathMax\(dq\f[R]
console.log(max.operator); \f[I]// \(aqmax\(aq\f[R]
console.log(max.values); \f[I]// CSSNumericArray {0: CSSUnitValue, 1: CSSUnitValue, 2: CSSUnitValue, length: 3}\f[R]
console.log(max.values[0]); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 10, unit: \(dqpx\(dq}\f[R]
.EE
.SS \f[CR]max()\f[R] representations
This example shows how \f[CR]max()\f[R] is represented by a
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] or a \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R], depending on whether
all of its arguments are absolute values.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqdemoBox\(dq>Text</\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
\f[CR]width\f[R] is set using a \f[CR]max()\f[R] whose arguments are all
absolute lengths, so the browser can resolve it to a single fixed value
immediately.
\f[CR]font\-size\f[R] is set using a \f[CR]max()\f[R] where one argument
uses the relative unit \f[CR]vw\f[R], so the browser can\(cqt resolve it
until layout (this will be represented by a \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R]).
.IP
.EX
demoBox {
  \f[B]width\f[R]: max(10px, 50px);
  \f[B]font\-size\f[R]: max(1rem, 5vw);
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
First we find the demo box\(cqs style rule and read its \f[CR]width\f[R]
and \f[CR]font\-size\f[R] values using \f[CR]styleMap\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] demoBox = document.querySelector(\(dq#demoBox\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] rules = document.getElementById(\(dqcss\-output\(dq).sheet.cssRules;
\f[B]const\f[R] rule = [...rules].find((r) \f[B]=>\f[R] r.selectorText === \(dq#demoBox\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] styleMap = rule.styleMap;
\f[B]const\f[R] width = styleMap.get(\(dqwidth\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] fontSize = styleMap.get(\(dqfont\-size\(dq);
.EE
.PP
We then log the type and value of the CSS Typed OM representations,
followed by the computed (resolved) values.
.IP
.EX
log(\(dqwidth\(dq);
log(\(ga type: ${width.constructor.name}\(ga);
log(\(ga value: ${width}\(ga);
log(\(ga resolved: ${getComputedStyle(demoBox).width}\(ga);

log(\(dq\(rsnfont\-size\(dq);
log(\(ga type: ${fontSize.constructor.name}\(ga);
log(\(ga values: [${[...fontSize.values].join(\(dq, \(dq)}]\(ga);
log(\(ga resolved: ${getComputedStyle(demoBox).fontSize}\(ga);
.EE
.SS Result
\f[CR]width\f[R] is represented by a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] object,
which has a value that matches the resolved width.
\f[CR]font\-size\f[R] is represented by a \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R] object
that exposes the \f[CR]max()\f[R] function\(cqs original operands.
